4. Pathological confirmation: The definitive diagnosis of ENE requires pathological confirmation through biopsy and examination of the lymph node tissue. This can be done through surgical biopsy or fine-needle needle biopsy.

5. Correlation with pathology: Imaging reports often report the presence of ENE based on imaging findings, but this must be correlated with pathological findings to confirm the diagnosis.

