The coefficient of friction (\( \mu \)) is a dimensionless quantity, meaning it has no units. It is a ratio of two forces, where the denominator is the normal force and the denominator is the frictional force.  
\[
\mu = \frac{f}{N}
\]  
The frictional force \( f \) has units of force, which are \([MLT^{-2}] \). The normal force \( N \) also has units of force, \([MLT^{-2}] \). Thus, the coefficient of friction is dimensionless:  
\[
\mu = \frac{[MLT^{-2}]}{[MLT^{-2}]} = [M^0L^0T^0]
\]  
