","A space group in crystallography is a mathematical description of the symmetry operations that can be applied to a crystal structure, leaving the crystal's appearance unchanged. It is the mathematical equivalent of the symmetry of a crystal lattice. The symmetry of a crystal structure is crucial for determining its physical properties, such as crystal growth, mechanical properties, and optical properties.

