","The key difference between σ (sigma) and π (pi) molecular orbitals lies in the distribution of electron density:  
1. σ (sigma) molecular orbitals have electron density directly above and below the internuclear bond.  
2. π (pi) molecular orbitals have electron density perpendicular to the internuclear bond, forming lobes above and below the bond.  

Thus, σ orbitals are symmetric with respect to the internuclear axis, while π orbitals are not.  

\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
&\text{σ orbital: Electron density directly above and below the internuclear bond, symmetric.} \\
&\text{π orbital: Electron density perpendicular to the internuclear bond, lobes above and below, asymmetric.}
\end{aligned}
