   - Thus, the recurrence relation is:  
     \[
     N(x) = 2N\left(\frac{x}{2}\right) + 1
     \]  

**Final Refined Formula:**  
The refined formula is:  
\[
N(x) = x + 1 \quad \text{for } x = 1 \quad \text{and} \quad
N(x) = 2N\left(\frac{x}{2}\right) + 1 \quad \text{for } x > 1
\]  

This recurrence relation represents the number of comparisons in the best-case scenario of QuickSort, where the pivot is always chosen such that it divides the list into two equal-length sublists.  

