\[
\Delta S = \frac{\Delta Q}{T}
\]
where \( \Delta Q \) is the heat added to the system and \( T \) is the temperature.

In this case, the work done by the friction force is \( F_{\text{fr}} v \), which is converted into heat energy. Thus, \( \Delta Q = F_{\text{fr}} v \). Substituting this into the entropy change equation:
\[
\Delta S = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T}
\]
The entropy production rate is the rate of entropy change, so:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{\partial S}{\partial t} = \frac{\Delta S}{\Delta t} = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T}
\]
Thus, the entropy production rate is:
\[
\boxed{\frac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T}}
