\]
The gain \( A_v \) decreases by 6 dB due to ageing. The new gain \( A_v' \) is:
\[
A_v' = \frac{A_v}{10^{6/10}} = \frac{100}{10^{0.6}} \approx 63.1 \text{ V/V}
\]
The new closed-loop voltage gain \( A_{vf}' \) is:
\[
A_{vf}' = \frac{A_v'}{1 + m_v A_v'} = \frac{63.1}{1 + 0.1 \times 63.1} = \frac{63.1}{7.31} \approx 8.64 \text{ V/V}
\]
The percentage change in the closed-loop gain is:
\[
\text{Percentage change} = \left( \frac{A_{vf}' - A_{vf}}{A_{vf}} \right) \times 100 = \left( \frac{8.64 - 9.09}{9.09} \right) \times 100 \approx -0.35\%
\]
Thus, the percentage change in the closed-loop gain is approximately \(\boxed{-0.35\%}\).",fluency,"# Task Description
