","The net chemical reaction for the discharging of a lead storage battery is:  
\[ \text{Pb} + \text{PbO}_2 + \4\text{H}^+ + 2\text{e}^- \rightarrow \text{PbSO}_4 + 2\text{H}_2\text{O} \]  
This reaction occurs at the anode (lead plate) and the cathode (lead dioxide plate), respectively. The overall reaction is the sum of the half-reactions.  

\[ \text{Pb} + \text{PbO}_2 + 4\text{H}^+ \rightarrow \text{PbSO}_4 + 2\text{H}_2\text{O} \]  

The overall reaction shows that lead (Pb) reacts with lead dioxide (PbO₂) in the presence of water (H⁺) to form lead sulfate (PbSO₄) and water (H₂O).  

\[ \boxed{\text{Pb} + \text{PbO}_2 + 4\text{H}^+ \rightarrow \text{PbSO}_4 + 2\text{H}_2\text{O}} \]",fluency,"# Task Description
