- \( \mu_0 = 4\pi \times 10^{-7} \, \text{T} \cdot \text{m/A} \) (permeability of free space),
- \( N = 100 \) (number of turns),
- \( I = 1 \, \text{A} \) (current),
- \( r = 0.2 \, \text{m} \) (radius of the coil).

Substituting the values:
\[
B = \frac{(4\pi \times 10^{-7} \, \text{T} \cdot \text{m/A}) \times 100 \times 1 \, \text{A}}{2 \pi \times 0.2 \, \text{m}} = \frac{4\pi \times 10^{-7} \times 100}{2 \pi \times 0.2} \, \text{T}
\]
\[
B = \frac{4 \times 10^{-5}}{0.4} \, \text{T} = 10^{-4} \, \text{T}
\]

Thus, the magnetic field strength at the center of the circular coil is \(\boxed{10^{-4} \, \text{T}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

