","The condition for constructive interference in a diffraction grating is:
\[
n \lambda = d \sin \theta
\]
where \( n \) is the order of the maximum, \( \lambda \) is the wavelength of the light, \( d \) is the slit separation, and \( \theta \) is the angle of the \( n \)-th order maximum.

1. **Calculate the slit separation \( d \):**
   \[
   d = \frac{1}{800 \text{ slits/mm}} = 1.25 \times 10^{-3} \text{ m} = 1.25 \times 10^{-6} \text{ m}
   \]

2. **For the third order maximum (\( n = 3 \)):**
   \[
   3 \times 600 \text{ nm} = 1.25 \times 10^{-3} \text{ m} \sin \theta_3
   \]
   \[
   1800 \times 10^{-9} \text{ m} = 1.25 \times 10^{-3} \text{ m} \sin \theta_3
   \]
   \[
   \sin \theta_3 = \frac{1800 \times 10^{-9}}{1.25 \times 10^{-3}} = 1.44 \text{ m}^{-1}
   \]
   \[
   \theta_3 = \sin^{-1}(1.44)
